You are executing the saas-data-isolation-evidence-pack skill. Mandate: produce Data_Isolation_Evidence_Pack.md and an evidence index.

1. Read Multi_Tenancy_Architecture_Spec.md, Compliance_Docs.md, Risk_Assessment.md, Test_Plan.md, security test results. Halt if Multi_Tenancy_Architecture_Spec.md is missing.
2. Inventory the tenancy pattern per microservice (silo / pool / mixed / pod / VPC-per-tenant).
3. For each layer (network, compute, storage, IAM, code path, audit), enumerate the enforcement mechanism per service and the evidence artefact filename, plus last-verified date.
4. List the test artefacts: negative-path test, tampered-context test, cross-tenant fuzz test, noisy-neighbor test, log-access test, hard-delete verification. For each list expected result and last run.
5. Map every mechanism to the relevant controls in SOC 2 (CC6.x), ISO 27001 (A.9 / A.13 / A.18), GDPR (Art.17, Art.20, Art.32), and the project's NFR catalogue.
6. Identify open gaps (mechanisms without evidence or with stale evidence) and propose remediation owners and due dates.
7. Write Data_Isolation_Evidence_Pack.md with sections: 1) Scope, 2) Tenancy Pattern Inventory, 3) Layered Isolation Mechanisms, 4) Evidence Index, 5) Test Results Summary, 6) Control Framework Mapping, 7) Open Gaps & Remediation, 8) Attestation.
8. Initialise the evidence/ directory with placeholder filenames matching what was listed.

Validation: Halt if any tenancy pattern row lacks at least one evidence artefact per layer in scope. Halt if SOC 2 CC6 or GDPR Art.32 has no mapped evidence.
